  "notes": "Label = board name (CircuitPython D/A name or callout name, preferring the one matching the silkscreen); functions = silkscreen spelling first, then chip pin, GPIO pin and other names read outward from the pin. Bare GPIO numbers (e.g. 26) are printed without a GPIO prefix, so not used as label. D/C pads matched to SWD/SWCLK by leader lines running up the board centre. Skipped LEDs, buttons, uUSB and status NeoPixels."
